60" y2="166"/><circle cx="251.8" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="251.8" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>early 3rd c.: The kingdom fragments among the Abhiras, Ikshvakus and Chutus</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">100 BCE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">220 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 100 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simuka">Simuka</a> founds the dynasty in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> (date disputed)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1st c. BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naganika">Naganika</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naneghat">Naneghat</a> inscription records <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satakarni-i">Satakarni I</a>'s horse sacrifices</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 125</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gautamiputra-satakarni">Gautamiputra Satakarni</a> destroys the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kshaharata-dynasty">Kshaharata dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahapana">Nahapana</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 150</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudradaman-i">Rudradaman I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-satraps">Western Satraps</a> twice defeats the Satavahanas</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">late 2nd c.</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yajna-sri-satakarni">Yajna Sri Satakarni</a> recovers parts of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">early 3rd c.</span><span class="rf-text">The kingdom fragments among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abhira-people">Abhiras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-ikshvakus">Ikshvakus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chutu-dynasty">Chutus</a></span></li></ol>
